    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d515">

                <pb facs="0563" n="459" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg459"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.00 Revolutions/155: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Culbertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-07-13T10:00:00-05:00">July 13, 1932—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>131. Peña Villalón has replaced Rios as Minister of the Interior which indicates
                    that the Radical Socialists have increased their influence in the
                    Government.</p>
                <pb facs="0564" n="460" xml:id="pg460"/>
                <p>The Minister of Hacienda yesterday issued a decree postponing until August 1st
                    the effectiveness of decree law No. 29 [<hi rendition="#italic">39</hi>] with
                    respect to foreign currency deposits in order to study a definite solution. (See
                    despatches Number 1179 and 1187).<anchor n="25" xml:id="d515-f1"/> In taking
                    this action the Minister referred to diplomatic protests against the law which
                    had been made by the representatives of the United States, England, France,
                    Italy and Spain.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
